          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 48-year-old woman presents with symmetrical swelling of MCP and PIP joints, DI</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 48-year-old woman presents with symmetrical swelling of MCP and PIP joints, DIP joints that appear normal, morning stiffness lasting two hours, and subcutaneous nodules over the elbows. Which investigation provides the HIGHEST specificity for her likely diagnosis?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Antinuclear antibody (ANA)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. ANA is primarily associated with systemic lupus erythematosus and other connective tissue diseases, not rheumatoid arthritis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Rheumatoid factor (RF)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. Although RF is positive in about 70% of RA cases, its specificity is lower than anti-CCP — RF can be elevated in chronic infections, liver disease, and even in healthy elderly individuals.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Anti-cyclic citrullinated peptide (anti-CCP) antibody</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Anti-CCP antibodies have approximately 95% specificity for rheumatoid arthritis and also predict more erosive disease, making them the investigation of choice when clinical features suggest RA.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>HLA-B27 typing</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. HLA-B27 is associated with ankylosing spondylitis and the seronegative spondyloarthropathies, not rheumatoid arthritis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Review this: the clinical picture here (symmetrical MCP/PIP, DIP sparing, nodules) points to RA, and among the serological tests, anti-CCP (~95% specificity) outperforms RF (~70% sensitivity but lower specificity)."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. Anti-CCP is the most specific serological marker for RA and helps predict disease severity — a key concept for clinical reasoning."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
                "enableSolutionsButton": true,
